.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The Berry-Tabor conjecture holds that a classically integrable system&#x27;s quantum energy levels, having no level repulsion mechanism to correlate them, behave locally like an uncorrelated (Poisson) point process -- in sharp contrast to a chaotic system&#x27;s GOE/GUE/GSE-type statistics. PoissonEnsemble realizes this null model directly (independent, uniformly spaced levels with no repulsion built in). Two statistics distinguish the two regimes:">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/images/thumb/sphx_glr_poisson_berry_tabor_demo_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/poisson_berry_tabor_demo`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Berry-Tabor Poisson Baseline</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/poisson_berry_tabor_demo`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Beyond nearest-neighbor spacing, the number variance \Sigma^2(L) -- the variance of the eigenvalue count in a randomly placed window of (unfolded) length L -- probes longer-range spectral correlations. An uncorrelated (Poisson) sequence has \Sigma^2(L) = L; level repulsion makes the Gaussian ensembles&#x27; spectra far more rigid, with only logarithmic growth (Dyson-Mehta 1963):">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/images/thumb/sphx_glr_rigidity_universality_demo_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/rigidity_universality_demo`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Spectral Rigidity and Universality</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/rmt/paper_replications/rigidity_universality_demo`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="For the Gaussian ensembles GOE (\beta=1), GUE (\beta=2), GSE (\beta=4), neighboring eigenvalues repel: small spacings are suppressed relative to a Poisson process. The (generalized) Wigner surmise, derived exactly from the eigenvalue spacing of a 2x2 beta-ensemble and normalized to unit mean spacing, models the nearest-neighbor spacing density (after unfolding to unit mean level density) as">

